"""openmesh-flash — flash OpenMesh firmware to supported LoRa boards from Linux.

Supports:
  * nRF52 boards with the Adafruit UF2 bootloader (Seeed T1000-E, RAK4631 solar,
    Seeed SenseCAP Solar Node P1): download the .uf2 and copy it to the mounted drive.
  * ESP32-S3 boards (Heltec Wireless Tracker): download the merged .bin and flash it with
    esptool over USB.

Design goals: Python 3.8+ standard library only, no root, no udev rules beyond the distro
defaults, friendly errors, and an explicit --dry-run that prints exactly what would happen.

Examples:
  openmesh-flash --list
  openmesh-flash --board auto --dry-run
  openmesh-flash --board t1000e
  openmesh-flash --board heltec_tracker --port /dev/ttyACM0
  openmesh-flash --board seeed_solar --file ./openmesh-seeed_solar.uf2 --sha256 <hex>
"""

